design:
Strategy: Modify the Cli struct to use subcommands for read/write while keeping mcp. The existing cmd_input and cmd_output functions remain untouched — only the parsing and dispatch in main() changes.

New Cli struct:
```rust
struct Cli {
    #[command(subcommand)]
    command: Commands,
}

enum Commands {
    /// Create a FIFO and read messages from writers
    Read {
        path: PathBuf,
        #[arg(short = 'l', long = "linger")]
        linger: bool,
        #[arg(short = 't', long = "timeout", value_name = "SECS")]
        timeout: Option<u64>,
    },
    /// Poll for a FIFO and write a message to it
    Write {
        path: PathBuf,
        #[arg(short = 't', long = "timeout", value_name = "SECS")]
        timeout: Option<u64>,
        message: Option<String>,
    },
    /// Start an MCP server over stdio
    Mcp,
}
```

The main() dispatch becomes:
```rust
match cli.command {
    Commands::Read { path, linger, timeout } => cmd_input(&path, timeout, linger),
    Commands::Write { path, timeout, message } => cmd_output(&path, message.as_deref(), timeout),
    Commands::Mcp => { ... }
}
```
